tools.description:
Edit one Pro Flash image at its unchanged native canvas size.

Supply image_url (preferred), image_base64, or an owned source_image_id.
method=text requires description; method=reference requires reference_image
({url}, {base64}, or {source_image_id}). References must fit the source canvas.
No-background defaults to the source's transparency. Optional palette
correction matches source colors. Query get_pro_flash_capabilities for exact
shapes. Returns one queued image; poll get_image(job_id), then download.

Cost: by the SOURCE canvas's longest side — 5 generations up to 96px, 6 from
100 to 208, 9 from 212 to 256, for one image. The same ladder as Pro Flash
create and inpaint, and cheaper than edit_image's 10/15/25 tier at every
size. get_pro_flash_capabilities(operation="edit", width=, height=) prices
an exact size for free.

PixelLab AI-powered pixel art generation service.

Use of this service is subject to PixelLab's Terms of Service:
https://pixellab.ai/termsofservice

This MCP server provides programmatic access to generate:
- Characters with multiple directional views
- Character animations
- Isometric tiles
- Top-down tilesets for game maps
- Sidescroller tilesets for platformer games

All generation operations are non-blocking and return job IDs for status tracking.
Requires PixelLab subscription (with credit fallback support).

**Pixel tools (free, exact, you are the artist)**: one command line, pixelart_workbench(argv=[...]), inspects, edits, draws and animates pixel art by your own decisions; combine it with the AI tools above. Start with pixelart_workbench(argv=['describe', 'start'], mode='low'|'high') — low acts directly with few tokens, high plans out loud and reviews every frame. Animated effects (spells, hits, explosions, auras): vfx_workbench(argv=['describe', 'start']) — same ids, exports to the user's My effects.

**Git access**: Clone and push game project source code with standard git.
Use `list_projects` to see your projects and their git clone URLs.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__pixellab__edit_image_pro_flash(args: {
  description?: string | null;
  image_base64?: string | null;
  image_url?: string | null;
  method?: "text" | "reference";
  no_background?: boolean | null;
  project_id?: string | null;
  // Exactly ONE of its three sources (`url` also accepts an `upload:<id>` from get_upload_url or a data: URL). Required when method='reference'. It must fit the edit canvas, which is the source image's own size because Pro Flash never rescales — crop it instead.
  reference_image?: {
  base64?: string | null;
  source_image_id?: string | null;
  url?: string | null;
  // How this reference should guide appearance.
  usage_description?: string | null;
} | null;
  seed?: number;
  source_image_id?: string | null;
  use_color_palette_correction?: boolean;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```
